Quick care summary and tips:
- Light: 6–8 hours direct sunlight or a very bright south-/west-facing windowsill. Supplemental grow light if light is limited.
- Soil & pot: Well-draining potting mix; pot with drainage holes. A 6–8" pot for one plant, larger if you want multiple stems.
- Watering: Keep soil evenly moist but not soggy. Water when the top ~1" feels dry; avoid letting the plant sit in water.
- Temperature & humidity: 65–85°F (18–29°C). Prefers moderate humidity; avoid cold drafts.
- Feeding: Light balanced fertilizer (half-strength) every 4–6 weeks during the growing season.
- Pruning & harvesting: Pinch or trim the top leaves regularly to encourage bushier growth. Never remove more than ~1/3 of foliage at once. You can begin harvesting baby leaves in 3–4 weeks; fuller harvests in 6–8+ weeks.
- Common problems: Yellowing leaves → overwatering; leggy growth → not enough light; watch for aphids or whiteflies and treat with insecticidal soap if needed.

